        "reasoning_content": "I'm comparing CPU bring-up ordering across architectures: on x86, sibling maps are set before notify_cpu_starting runs, whereas on s390 update_cpu_masks() happens after notify_cpu_starting, meaning the sibling cpumask isn't populated until later in the boot sequence.\n\nBy contrast x86 explicitly calls set_cpu_sibling_map(cpu) before notify_cpu_starting, guaranteeing topology masks are current when sched_core_cpu_starting consumes cpu_smt_mask - x86's code even comments that topology info must be up to date before notify_cpu_starting(). s390 lacks this guarantee since update_cpu_masks() runs afterward, so this looks like a genuine ordering contract violation worth writing up.\n\n这个拓扑表被sched_core_cpu_starting消费，用于识别同组smt cpu构建core调度组。x86明确保证mask先于notify更新，但s390是否有同等保证尚不明确，消费时刻可能拿到更新前的陈旧状态，具体是否出问题取决于cpu_topology初始状态和thread_mask的持久性——我需要检查目标架构进入sched_cpu_starting前是否已调用对应的topology mask更新函数，尤其是该cpu之前经历过热插拔重启的情况。\n\nthread_mask在update_cpu_masks调用前的初始或残留值仍不清楚，s390这种调用次序是否会造成实际功能问题也还无法确定。\n\n",
